  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 UNDP GRANT INCLUSIVE DIGITAL TRANSFORMATI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Inclusive Digital Transformation for Malawi succeeds the National Registration and Identification System (NRIS) (October 2016 to June 2024) and the projetis about establihing digital ID and CRVS system that is accessible to all including people with disablities, women, youth and elderly with a goal of leving no one behind. NRIS ensured the right to identity and citizenship, aligning with SDG 16 for universal legal identity for all by 2030. In collaboration with the National Registration Bureau (NRB), the NRIS project provided unique registration for Malawians aged 16 and above, issuing identity cards and establishing management information systems (MIS) as central reference for planning and individual identity. It is the MIS that will contribute to a robust Digital Public Infrastructure where Malawians will access digital public goods (DPGs) (services).</narrative>
  </description>
